  "notes": "USAGE:\n- 〜が{慕|した}わしい (to feel fond longing for ~)\n- {慕|した}わしい{人|ひと} (a beloved person)\n- {慕|した}わしさ (noun form: fondness, longing)\nA literary and somewhat formal word expressing warm, nostalgic affection. Often used for things one cannot be with or have lost—distant memories, deceased loved ones, or places left behind.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {慕|した}う (verb: to yearn for, admire)\n- {懐|なつ}かしい (nostalgic)\n- {恋|こい}しい (longed-for, missed)",
